    "id": "3385272677",
    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "ASCII BOP!!! (+CUSTOMIZE)",
    "description": "WARNING: This wallpaper may potentially trigger seizures for people with photosensitive epilepsy.\n\nMy first non-video wallpaper! Made using noise refraction visuals alongside an ASCII Filter. I've also added an audio-responsive visualizer and background. This was way more fun to make than I'd thought it would be.\n\nCurrent possible customizations for this wallpaper are:\n- Audio Visualizer (With size, position, spacing, color, and bar count sliders)\n- Audio-Responsive BG (With intensity scale)\n- Background Transparency\n- ASCII Color\n- Chromatic Abberation\n- Remove ASCII filter (not sure why you would do this but now you can!)\n- RAINBOW MODE (Variable scroll speed)\n- 3 Different Noise Backgrounds, those being:\n     - Voronoi (Default)\n     - Worley\n     - Perlin\n\nNOTE: You can turn off the visualizer or the audio-responsive background with the checkmarks \"Audio Visualizer\" and \"Audio-Responsive BG\" in the settings.\n\n[11/10/25] UPDATE: WOW Lots of people have checked out this wallpaper! \nI can't add as many features and suggestions as I want unfortunately as I'm still not well-versed in wallpaper engine, but I hope a small patch with a few additions and fixes will suffice.\nThis probably marks the final update to the wallpaper as I never actually planned to upkeep a wallpaper like this, apologies if this means a feature you wished this wallpaper had will never be included.\n\nThis was a small side project I took up for fun last year but to see so many people using this really warms my heart. Thanks again for reading and using my wallpaper :)\n\n- [ ]",
